      "text": "This intelligent question was raised by @OgechiMiracle4 as comment under my Day 10 post, and I'll be glad to explain to the Bless community at large.\n\nMost people don’t realize this... ✴️\n\nWhen you run a node on @theblessnetwork , you're not just “mining” or staking, you’re literally powering a shared global computer.\n\nHere's what that actually means \n\n1️⃣ Apps like AI tools, websites, or games need compute to run, basically, digital “muscle” to process data.\n\nTraditionally, they rent it from AWS or Google Cloud. That’s centralized, expensive, and gatekept.\n\n2️⃣ Bless flips that model.\n\nInstead of one giant data center, it breaks compute into tiny jobs, and spreads them across regular people’s devices (like yours).\n\nYour laptop becomes a mini server.\nSo does someone’s console in Lagos...or a smart TV in Manila.\n\n3️⃣ When you run a Bless node, you're offering spare processing power from your device to help execute these jobs.\n\n▶️ AI models? Rendered through you.\n▶️ Website traffic? Routed through you.\nAll secured, sandboxed, and privacy-safe.\n\n4️⃣ The more stable and responsive your node, the more work it can take on... and the more $TIME points you earn.\n\nThis is compute as a community resource.\nIt’s like Airbnb for processing power.\n\n5️⃣ The vision?\nA truly decentralized internet, not just in theory, but in function. One where everyday people own the infrastructure, not just use it.\n\nYou’re not just part of the network.\nYou are the network.\n\nPlease repost 🔁 and educate more people",
